module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExtensionByZeroQuasiCompact
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartTransitionCompatibility

/-!
# Determination of the components of the chart transport of Stacks 07UM

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B`, let
`ℐ ⊆ 𝒪_X` be a sheaf of ideals which is cartesian on affine charts, let `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)` be the
open complement, let `𝒢` and `ℱ` be `𝒪_X`-modules and let `θ : 𝒢|_U ⟶ ℱ|_U`.  Step 2 of the
surjectivity argument for [Stacks, Tag 07UM] transports `θ` to an étale scheme chart `A` of `X`,
applies the first display of [Stacks, Tag 01YB] on the chart's scheme, and carries the resulting
morphism back as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha`, a morphism `α : (ℐᵏ𝒢)|_A ⟶ ℱ|_A` of the
restrictions to the slice of the small étale site of `X` at `A`.

Step 3 has to know what the components of `α` are at the charts of `X` lying over `U`, and not
only at the charts cut out by the Zariski opens of the chart's scheme.  **Naturality of `α` does
not answer this.**  Along a morphism `r : Z ⟶ openChart … A V` of charts,
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply` pins the component of `α` at `Z` only on the
image of the restriction map of `ℐᵏ𝒢` along `r`, which is in general a proper submodule of the
sections over `Z`; it is a constraint, not a determination.

This file determines the component.  The mechanism is base change, not naturality: over an
*affine* open `Ω` of the scheme of `Z` lying over an *affine* open `V` of the scheme of `A`, the
sections of a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module over the chart cut out by `Ω` are *generated*, over the
functions on `Ω`, by the restrictions of the sections over the chart cut out by `V` — this is
Descent, Proposition 03DX (2), in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.bijective_sectionsBaseChange_openChartRestrict` read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top`.  Such pairs `(V, Ω)` with
`V` off the support of the chartwise sheaf of ideals cover the scheme of `Z`, because a chart
lying over `U` lies entirely off that support; and separatedness of `ℱ` glues the resulting local
agreements.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.asStructureSheafModule` is an `𝒪_X`-module retyped over
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureRingSheaf`, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlphaSheaf` is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha` retyped the
  same way; see the implementation notes.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartFamily` is a candidate family for the components of a morphism of
  the restrictions to the slice at a chart — a map on the sections over every étale chart of `X`
  identified with the postcomposition of a chart of `U` — and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartFamily.IsNatural` its compatibility with restriction.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowChartFamily` is the candidate family the transport of `θ`
  provides: the inclusion `ℐᵏ𝒢 ⟶ 𝒢` followed by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.homOnChart`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_support_compl_of_pc_eq`: **an étale chart of `X` lying over
  `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)` lies entirely off the support of the chartwise sheaf of ideals.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_affineOpens_le_preimage`: **the affine cover.**  Every point of
  the scheme of such a chart `Z` over a chart `W` has an affine open neighbourhood lying over an
  affine open of the scheme of `W` off the support.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.val_app_eq_of_map`: the two sides agree on the sections restricted
  from the larger chart — naturality of `α` and of the candidate family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.val_app_eq_of_affineOpens`: **they agree on all of the sections over
  the chart cut out by an affine open lying over an affine open off the support**, those sections
  being generated by the restricted ones.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.val_app_eq_of_pc_eq`: **the component determination**, for an
  arbitrary candidate family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.val_app_eq_homOnChart` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha_val_app_eq_homOnChart`: **the component determination for
  the transport of `θ`, and for the morphism `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha` produces.**

## Implementation notes

**The base case is a hypothesis, not a result.**  Every determination statement below takes as a
hypothesis `hbase` that the component of `α` at the chart cut out by a Zariski open of the
chart's scheme off the support is the transport of `θ` there.  For
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha` that base case is *not* proved here: it is the component
formula `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartSectionsLinearEquiv_chartSchemeModuleHomEquiv_symm_apply`
read at `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartPush`, and it is discharged in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ChartAlphaBaseCase.lean`, whose
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlphaSheaf_val_app_openChartInclusion_eq_complementHomOnChart` is
exactly the `hbase` which
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha_val_app_eq_homOnChart` below asks for.  Nothing below
depends on it, and the determination is exactly the step which the base case alone does not
give.

**The structure sheaf has two spellings and only one of them works on the slice.**
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules` is indexed by the structure sheaf of the small étale *ringed
site*, whose type names `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.J` of it;
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureRingSheaf` has the same value but its type names
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.topology`.  At the first spelling instance search does not
find the `CategoryTheory.Category` structure of `CategoryTheory.Over` of a chart — the site is a
projection of a `def` — so `α.val.app (op (Over.mk h))` cannot even be elaborated.  The two
spellings are definitionally equal, so `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.asStructureSheafModule` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlphaSheaf` are `abbrev`s with no content: their only job is to put
the good spelling into the *declared* type, which a type ascription on the argument does not do.

**Every equation is passed to a `congrArg` or an `Eq.trans`, never rewritten.**  The sections of a
module on the slice at a chart over `Over.mk h` are the sections over `h`'s source, and the
restriction maps agree, but only definitionally: `(N.over W).val.map m.op` and
`N.val.map m.left.op` are different terms, as are `CategoryTheory.ConcreteCategory.hom` and
`CategoryTheory.ModuleCat.Hom.hom` of one and the same morphism.  A `rw` there reports a missing
pattern; an `Eq.trans` discharges it by a definitional check.

**The span is taken at the slice spelling of both the ring and the module.**  In
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.val_app_eq_of_affineOpens` the generating family comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top`, which names the ring as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing` and the module as the sections over the étale chart, whereas
the two maps being compared are linear over the sections of the structure sheaf of the slice.  The
`CategoryTheory.Submodule.span_induction` is therefore run on a restatement of that equality at the
slice spelling: with the two mixed, the scalar action in the `smul` case has no instance.

**No hypothesis beyond what the mathematics needs.**  Quasi-coherence of the source is used, and
only through Descent, Proposition 03DX (2), which is unconditional here
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.bijective_sectionsBaseChange_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`); affineness of
the opens is a choice of open, not a hypothesis; separatedness of the target is the `isSheaf`
field it carries.  Nothing is assumed about the chart identification.  No declaration here
carries a `stacks` tag: this is an input to [Stacks, Tag 07UM], not an assertion of it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03EM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03EM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04M0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04M0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07UM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07UM)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (I : IdealSheaves B S hS X.1 X.2)

/-! ### A chart of the open complement lies off the support -/

/-- **A point of an étale chart of `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)`, pushed into `X`, lies in the unit locus of
`ℐ`.**  The structure morphism of the chart factors through the inclusion of `U`, whose image on
points is the unit locus.

This restates a `private` declaration of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoherentHomColimitOverComplement.lean`. -/
theorem mem_idealUnitLocus_pc_of_points
    (P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1)
    (y : points B S hS
      (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj (pc B S hS X I P)))) :
    pointsMap B S hS
        (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj (pc B S hS X I P)))
        (pc B S hS X I P).1.hom y ∈ idealUnitLocus B S hS X I := by
  have h2 : pointsMap B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1
      (idealComplementι B S hS X I).hom
      (pointsMap B S hS
        (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1).obj P))
        P.1.hom y) ∈ idealUnitLocus B S hS X I :=
    (range_pointsMap_ι_openSubspaceOfPoints B S hS (F := X.1)
      (idealUnitLocus B S hS X I)).le ⟨_, rfl⟩
  show pointsMap B S hS
      (yoneda.obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1).obj P))
      (P.1.hom ≫ (idealComplementι B S hS X I).hom) y ∈ idealUnitLocus B S hS X I
  rw [pointsMap_comp]
  exact h2

variable (hIc : IsCartesianOnAffineCharts I.toSheafOfModules)

/-- **Every point of an étale chart of `X` underlying a chart of `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)` lies off the
support of the chartwise sheaf of ideals.**

The chart is a parameter with an equation, so that a consumer which has only an identification
of its chart with a postcomposition — the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_pc_eq_of_over` produces — can use this directly. -/
theorem mem_support_compl_of_pc_eq
    {P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1} {Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (hP : pc B S hS X I P = Z) (x : chartScheme Z) :
    x ∈ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc Z).support.compl : (chartScheme Z).Opens) := by
  subst hP
  refine mem_support_compl_of_mem_chartUnitLocusPreimage B S hS X I hIc _ x ?_
  exact (mem_chartUnitLocusPreimage_iff_pointsMap B S hS X I _ x).2
    (mem_idealUnitLocus_pc_of_points B S hS X I P _)

/-! ### The affine cover of a chart of the open complement over a chart -/

/-- **An affine pair over a point of a chart lying over a chart of `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)`.**  Given a
morphism of charts `h : Z ⟶ W` with `Z` underlying a chart of `U`, every point of the scheme of
`Z` has an affine open neighbourhood which lies over an affine open of the scheme of `W` off the
support of the chartwise sheaf of ideals.

This is the cover over which the component determination is local: the affine opens of a scheme
are a basis, and the complement of the support at `Z` is the whole of the scheme of `Z` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_support_compl_of_pc_eq`. -/
theorem exists_affineOpens_le_preimage
    {P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1} {Z W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (hP : pc B S hS X I P = Z) (h : Z ⟶ W) (x : chartScheme Z) :
    ∃ (V : (chartScheme W).affineOpens) (Ω : (chartScheme Z).affineOpens),
      V.1 ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl :
          (chartScheme W).Opens) ∧
        x ∈ Ω.1 ∧ Ω.1 ≤ chartSchemeMap h ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 := by
  have hx : x ∈ chartSchemeMap h ⁻¹ᵁ
      ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl : (chartScheme W).Opens) :=
    (support_compl_idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc h).le
      (mem_support_compl_of_pc_eq B S hS X I hIc hP x)
  obtain ⟨V, hVmem, hxV, hVle⟩ :=
    TopologicalSpace.Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp (chartScheme W).isBasis_affineOpens
      (show (chartSchemeMap h).base x ∈
        ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl :
          (chartScheme W).Opens) from hx)
  obtain ⟨Ω, hΩmem, hxΩ, hΩle⟩ :=
    TopologicalSpace.Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp (chartScheme Z).isBasis_affineOpens
      (show x ∈ chartSchemeMap h ⁻¹ᵁ V from hxV)
  exact ⟨⟨V, hVmem⟩, ⟨Ω, hΩmem⟩, hVle, hxΩ, hΩle⟩

/-! ### The component determination -/

/-- An `𝒪_X`-module, typed over `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureRingSheaf`.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules` is indexed by the structure sheaf of the small étale *ringed
site*, whose type names a projection of that site; the two spellings are definitionally equal, but
only at the second does instance search find the `CategoryTheory.Category` structure of
`CategoryTheory.Over` of a chart — and without it a component of a morphism of the restrictions to
the slice at a chart cannot even be written down. -/
abbrev asStructureSheafModule (M : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf B S hS X) := M

variable (N₁ N₂ : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf B S hS X))

/-- A candidate family for the components of a morphism of the restrictions to the slice of the
small étale site at a chart: a map on the sections over every étale chart of `X` which is
identified with the postcomposition of a chart of `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)`. -/
abbrev ChartFamily : Type _ :=
  ∀ (P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1) (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1),
    pc B S hS X I P = Q → (N₁.val.obj (op Q) ⟶ N₂.val.obj (op Q))

/-- Compatibility of a candidate family with restriction along an arbitrary morphism of étale
charts of `X` between two charts identified with postcompositions of charts of `U`. -/
def ChartFamily.IsNatural (τ : ChartFamily B S hS X I N₁ N₂) : Prop :=
  ∀ (P' P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1)
    (Q' Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (hP' : pc B S hS X I P' = Q')
    (hP : pc B S hS X I P = Q) (m : Q' ⟶ Q) (x : N₁.val.obj (op Q)),
      (τ P' Q' hP').hom (N₁.val.map m.op x) = N₂.val.map m.op ((τ P Q hP).hom x)

/-- **The component determination on a section restricted from the larger chart.**  Over a
Zariski open of the smaller chart's scheme lying over a Zariski open of the larger one off the
support, the two sides agree on every section restricted from there: the naturality of `α` in the
slice at the chart and the naturality of the candidate family both reduce the statement to the
base case.

The morphism of charts along which the section is restricted is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.openChartHomOfLE` followed by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.openChartRestrict`, which is the one sitting in the square over `h`. -/
theorem val_app_eq_of_map {W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (α : N₁.over W ⟶ N₂.over W)
    (τ : ChartFamily B S hS X I N₁ N₂) (hτ : ChartFamily.IsNatural B S hS X I N₁ N₂ τ)
    (hbase : ∀ (V : (chartScheme W).Opens)
      (hV : V ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl :
        (chartScheme W).Opens))
      (y : N₁.val.obj (op (openChart B S hS X.1 W V))),
        (α.val.app (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 W V)))).hom y =
          (τ (idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV) (openChart B S hS X.1 W V)
            (pc_idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV)).hom y)
    {Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : Z ⟶ W)
    {V : (chartScheme W).Opens} {Ω : (chartScheme Z).Opens}
    (hV : V ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl : (chartScheme W).Opens))
    (hΩV : Ω ≤ chartSchemeMap h ⁻¹ᵁ V)
    (P' : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1)
    (hP' : pc B S hS X I P' = openChart B S hS X.1 Z Ω)
    (z : N₁.val.obj (op (openChart B S hS X.1 W V))) :
    (α.val.app (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z Ω ≫ h)))).hom
        (N₁.val.map
          (openChartHomOfLE B S hS X.1 Z hΩV ≫ openChartRestrict B S hS X.1 h V).op z) =
      (τ P' (openChart B S hS X.1 Z Ω) hP').hom
        (N₁.val.map
          (openChartHomOfLE B S hS X.1 Z hΩV ≫ openChartRestrict B S hS X.1 h V).op z) := by
  let f := openChartHomOfLE B S hS X.1 Z hΩV ≫ openChartRestrict B S hS X.1 h V
  have hα' := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply α.val
    (Over.homMk f
      (openChartHomOfLE_comp_openChartRestrict_comp_openChartInclusion
        B S hS X.1 h V hΩV) :
      Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z Ω ≫ h) ⟶
        Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 W V)).op z
  exact hα'.trans ((congrArg (fun w => N₂.val.map f.op w) (hbase V hV z)).trans
    (hτ P' (idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV) (openChart B S hS X.1 Z Ω)
      (openChart B S hS X.1 W V) hP' (pc_idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV)
      f z).symm)

/-- **The component determination over an affine open lying over an affine open off the
support.**  The sections of a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module over the chart cut out by an affine
open of the smaller chart's scheme are generated, over the functions on that open, by the
restrictions of the sections over the chart cut out by an affine open of the larger chart's
scheme — Descent, Proposition 03DX (2) — and both sides are linear, so
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.val_app_eq_of_map` suffices. -/
theorem val_app_eq_of_affineOpens (hN₁ : N₁.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    {W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (α : N₁.over W ⟶ N₂.over W)
    (τ : ChartFamily B S hS X I N₁ N₂) (hτ : ChartFamily.IsNatural B S hS X I N₁ N₂ τ)
    (hbase : ∀ (V : (chartScheme W).Opens)
      (hV : V ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl :
        (chartScheme W).Opens))
      (y : N₁.val.obj (op (openChart B S hS X.1 W V))),
        (α.val.app (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 W V)))).hom y =
          (τ (idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV) (openChart B S hS X.1 W V)
            (pc_idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV)).hom y)
    {Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : Z ⟶ W)
    {V : (chartScheme W).Opens} {Ω : (chartScheme Z).Opens}
    (hVaff : IsAffineOpen V) (hΩaff : IsAffineOpen Ω)
    (hV : V ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl : (chartScheme W).Opens))
    (hΩV : Ω ≤ chartSchemeMap h ⁻¹ᵁ V)
    (P' : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1)
    (hP' : pc B S hS X I P' = openChart B S hS X.1 Z Ω)
    (y : (N₁.over W).val.obj (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z Ω ≫ h)))) :
    (α.val.app (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z Ω ≫ h)))).hom y =
      (τ P' (openChart B S hS X.1 Z Ω) hP').hom y := by
  let f := openChartHomOfLE B S hS X.1 Z hΩV ≫ openChartRestrict B S hS X.1 h V
  let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := X.2) f
  let _ := chartSectionsModule N₁ f
  have _ := chartSections_isScalarTower N₁ f
  have hspan := (chartBaseChange_surjective_iff_span_eq_top N₁ f).1
    (bijective_sectionsBaseChange_openChartRestrict B S hS X.1 X.2 N₁ hN₁ h
      hVaff hΩaff hΩV).2
  have hspan' : Submodule.span
      (↑(((structureRingSheaf B S hS X).over W).obj.obj
        (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z Ω ≫ h)))))
      (Set.range (fun w : ((N₁.over W).val.obj
            (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 W V))) : Type u) =>
          N₁.val.map f.op w) :
        Set ((N₁.over W).val.obj
          (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z Ω ≫ h))) : Type u)) = ⊤ := hspan
  have hy := hspan'.ge (Submodule.mem_top (x := y))
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := hx
      exact val_app_eq_of_map B S hS X I hIc N₁ N₂ α τ hτ hbase h hV hΩV P' hP' w
  | zero => exact (map_zero _).trans (map_zero _).symm
  | add x₁ x₂ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      refine (map_add _ x₁ x₂).trans (Eq.trans ?_ (map_add _ x₁ x₂).symm)
      exact congrArg₂ (fun p q => p + q) ih₁ ih₂
  | smul b x _ ih =>
      refine (map_smul _ b x).trans (Eq.trans ?_ (map_smul _ b x).symm)
      exact congrArg (fun z => b • z) ih

/-- **The component determination.**  Let `α` be a morphism of the restrictions to the slice of
the small étale site of `X` at a chart `W`, let `τ` be a candidate family on the charts lying
over `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)`, compatible with restriction, and suppose that the component of `α` at the
chart cut out by a Zariski open of the scheme of `W` off the support agrees with `τ` there.  Then
the component of `α` at *every* chart of `X` lying over `U` and over `W` is `τ`.

The two sides agree after restriction to the charts cut out by an affine open cover of the
scheme of the smaller chart chosen inside the preimages of affine opens off the support — that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.val_app_eq_of_affineOpens` — and the target is a sheaf, hence separated,
so they agree. -/
theorem val_app_eq_of_pc_eq (hN₁ : N₁.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    {W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (α : N₁.over W ⟶ N₂.over W)
    (τ : ChartFamily B S hS X I N₁ N₂) (hτ : ChartFamily.IsNatural B S hS X I N₁ N₂ τ)
    (hbase : ∀ (V : (chartScheme W).Opens)
      (hV : V ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl :
        (chartScheme W).Opens))
      (y : N₁.val.obj (op (openChart B S hS X.1 W V))),
        (α.val.app (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 W V)))).hom y =
          (τ (idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV) (openChart B S hS X.1 W V)
            (pc_idealComplementChart B S hS X I hIc W V hV)).hom y)
    {P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1} {Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (hP : pc B S hS X I P = Z) (h : Z ⟶ W) (y : N₁.val.obj (op Z)) :
    (α.val.app (op (Over.mk h))).hom y = (τ P Z hP).hom y := by
  choose V Ω hV hxΩ hΩV using fun x : chartScheme Z =>
    exists_affineOpens_le_preimage B S hS X I hIc hP h x
  have hcov : ⨆ x, (Ω x).1 = ⊤ := by
    refine eq_top_iff.2 fun z _ => ?_
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨z, hxΩ z⟩
  refine (Presieve.isSeparatedFor_iff_generate.2
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isSeparated_presheaf N₂ _
      (ofArrows_openChartInclusion_mem_topology B S hS X.1 Z
        (fun x => (Ω x).1) hcov))).ext ?_
  rintro Y g ⟨x⟩
  obtain ⟨P'', hP''⟩ := exists_pc_eq_of_over B S hS X I
    (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z (Ω x).1 ≫ eqToHom hP.symm)
  have hαn := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply α.val
    (Over.homMk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z (Ω x).1) rfl :
      Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z (Ω x).1 ≫ h) ⟶ Over.mk h).op y
  have haff := val_app_eq_of_affineOpens B S hS X I hIc N₁ N₂ hN₁ α τ hτ hbase h
    (V x).2 (Ω x).2 (hV x) (hΩV x) P'' hP''
    (N₁.val.map (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z (Ω x).1).op y)
  have hτn := hτ P'' P (openChart B S hS X.1 Z (Ω x).1) Z hP'' hP
    (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 Z (Ω x).1) y
  exact hαn.symm.trans (haff.trans hτn)

/-! ### The component determination for the transport of `θ` -/

variable (G F : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (θ : (restrictToIdealComplement B S hS X I).obj G ⟶
      (restrictToIdealComplement B S hS X I).obj F)

/-- **The candidate family for the components of the morphism which the chart transport
produces**: the inclusion `ℐᵏ𝒢 ⟶ 𝒢` followed by the transport of `θ` to the chart. -/
def idealPowChartFamily (k : ℕ) :
    ChartFamily B S hS X I (idealPowModule I k G) F :=
  fun _ Q hP =>
    (idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app (op Q) ≫ homOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hP

/-- **The candidate family commutes with restriction along an arbitrary morphism of étale charts
of `X` between two charts lying over `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)`.**

The inclusion `ℐᵏ𝒢 ⟶ 𝒢` is a morphism of modules, so it commutes with restriction; and the
transport of `θ` commutes with restriction by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.homOnChart_naturality`,
the lift of the morphism of charts to the charts of `U` being supplied by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_pcMap_eq_of_pc_eq`. -/
theorem isNatural_idealPowChartFamily (k : ℕ) :
    ChartFamily.IsNatural B S hS X I (idealPowModule I k G) F
      (idealPowChartFamily B S hS X I G F θ k) := by
  intro P' P Q' Q hP' hP m x
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := exists_pcMap_eq_of_pc_eq B S hS X I hP' hP m
  have hι := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (idealPowModuleι I k G).val m.op x
  have hn := homOnChart_naturality B S hS X I G F θ hP' hP m l hl
    (((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app (op Q)).hom x)
  refine (Stacks.ModuleCat.comp_hom_apply ((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app (op Q'))
      (homOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hP') _).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (congrArg (fun z : F.val.obj (op Q) => F.val.map m.op z)
    (Stacks.ModuleCat.comp_hom_apply ((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app (op Q))
      (homOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hP) x).symm)
  exact (congrArg (fun z : G.val.obj (op Q') =>
    (homOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hP').hom z) hι).trans hn

/-- **Component determination for the morphism which the chart transport of Stacks 07UM
produces.**  Let `α` be a morphism of the restrictions to the slice of the small étale site of
`X` at an étale scheme chart `W` whose component at the chart cut out by a Zariski open of the
scheme of `W` off the support of the chartwise sheaf of ideals is the transport of `θ` there.
Then for *every* étale chart `Z` of `X` lying over `U = X ∖ V(ℐ)` and every morphism
`h : Z ⟶ W`, the component of `α` at `h` is the transport of `θ` at `Z`, precomposed with the
inclusion `ℐᵏ𝒢 ⟶ 𝒢`.

This **determines** the component — it is not merely a constraint on the image of a restriction
map, which is all that naturality of `α` gives: the sections of `ℐᵏ𝒢` over the chart cut out by
an affine open of the scheme of `Z` are *generated*, over the functions on that open, by the
restrictions of the sections over the chart cut out by an affine open of the scheme of `W` off
the support, by Descent, Proposition 03DX (2); and such opens cover the scheme of `Z`, because a
chart lying over `U` lies entirely off the support
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_support_compl_of_pc_eq`). Separatedness of `ℱ` glues the
resulting local agreements. -/
theorem val_app_eq_homOnChart (k : ℕ)
    (hIGq : (idealPowModule I k G).IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    {W : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (α : (asStructureSheafModule B S hS X (idealPowModule I k G)).over W ⟶
      (asStructureSheafModule B S hS X F).over W)
    (hbase : ∀ (V : (chartScheme W).Opens)
      (hV : V ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc W).support.compl :
        (chartScheme W).Opens))
      (y : (idealPowModule I k G).val.obj (op (openChart B S hS X.1 W V))),
        (α.val.app (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 W V)))).hom y =
          (complementHomOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hIc W V hV).hom
            (((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app
              (op (openChart B S hS X.1 W V))).hom y))
    {P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1} {Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (hP : pc B S hS X I P = Z) (h : Z ⟶ W)
    (y : (idealPowModule I k G).val.obj (op Z)) :
    (α.val.app (op (Over.mk h))).hom y =
      (homOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hP).hom
        (((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app (op Z)).hom y) :=
  (val_app_eq_of_pc_eq B S hS X I hIc (idealPowModule I k G) F hIGq α
      (idealPowChartFamily B S hS X I G F θ k)
      (isNatural_idealPowChartFamily B S hS X I G F θ k)
      (fun V hV y => (hbase V hV y).trans
        (Stacks.ModuleCat.comp_hom_apply _ _ y).symm) hP h y).trans
    (Stacks.ModuleCat.comp_hom_apply ((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app (op Z))
      (homOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hP) y)

/-- `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha`, typed over
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.structureRingSheaf`: the same morphism, at the spelling of the structure
sheaf at which a component on the slice of the small étale site at the chart can be written
down.  See `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.asStructureSheafModule`. -/
abbrev chartAlphaSheaf (hZt : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hN : IsNoetherian B S hS hZt X.1)
    (hIq : I.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (hFq : F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hG : IsCoherent B S hS X.1 X.2 G) (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (k : ℕ)
    (φ : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit.idealPowSmul
        (idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc A) k (chartPush B S hS X G A) ⟶
      chartPush B S hS X F A) :
    (asStructureSheafModule B S hS X (idealPowModule I k G)).over A ⟶
      (asStructureSheafModule B S hS X F).over A :=
  chartAlpha B S hS X I hIc G F hZt hN hIq hFq hG A k φ

/-- **The component determination for the morphism `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlpha`
produces.**  This is Step 3 of [Stacks, Tag 07UM] at the chart: once the component of the
morphism at the charts cut out by the Zariski opens of the chart's scheme off the support is
known to be the transport of `θ`, its component at *every* chart of `X` lying over
`U = X ∖ V(ℐ)` and over the chart is determined. -/
theorem chartAlpha_val_app_eq_homOnChart (hZt : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hN : IsNoetherian B S hS hZt X.1)
    (hIq : I.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (hFq : F.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hG : IsCoherent B S hS X.1 X.2 G) (A : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (k : ℕ)
    (φ : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerColimit.idealPowSmul
        (idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc A) k (chartPush B S hS X G A) ⟶
      chartPush B S hS X F A)
    (hbase : ∀ (V : (chartScheme A).Opens)
      (hV : V ≤ ((idealSheafDataOfChart B S hS X I hIc A).support.compl :
        (chartScheme A).Opens))
      (y : (idealPowModule I k G).val.obj (op (openChart B S hS X.1 A V))),
        ((chartAlphaSheaf B S hS X I hIc G F hZt hN hIq hFq hG A k φ).val.app
            (op (Over.mk (openChartInclusion B S hS X.1 A V)))).hom y =
          (complementHomOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hIc A V hV).hom
            (((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app
              (op (openChart B S hS X.1 A V))).hom y))
    {P : SmallEtale B S hS (idealComplement B S hS X I).1} {Z : SmallEtale B S hS X.1}
    (hP : pc B S hS X I P = Z) (h : Z ⟶ A)
    (y : (idealPowModule I k G).val.obj (op Z)) :
    ((chartAlphaSheaf B S hS X I hIc G F hZt hN hIq hFq hG A k φ).val.app
        (op (Over.mk h))).hom y =
      (homOnChart B S hS X I G F θ hP).hom
        (((idealPowModuleι I k G).val.app (op Z)).hom y) :=
  val_app_eq_homOnChart B S hS X I hIc G F θ k
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_idealPowModule B S hS X I G hZt hN hIq hG k)
    (chartAlphaSheaf B S hS X I hIc G F hZt hN hIq hFq hG A k φ) hbase hP h y

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
